eah she got  rocked a couple times that could have  changed the whole aspect of the fight um  who knows how she recovered off those uh  knockdowns early in the first round  and  there's girls that would have literally  laid there and got taken down or gave up  like amanda did the first fight  so for all you people saying oh wow she  didn't deserve it blah blah blah like  juliana won the first fight by finish  man i know you just didn't so that's why  i deserve a trilogy fight  you could say what the score was  50 44 50 43  but  that doesn't  talk about the whole fight there was  moments in that fight where juliana  could have won that fight  um  and just want to give out huge respect  for her amanda i feel like  getting too cocky she's getting a little  arrogant saying oh i could have went  five rounds if i could have finished her  in the first round if i wanted to uh but  i wanted to go five rounds so i could  show her who's better blah blah blah get  out of here with that you couldn't  finish her i think emmanuel amanda  started taking her down in the third  fourth and fifth round because  she didn't want to get caught again on  the feet she knows that uh juliana  punches hard her eye was very swollen  she was on crutches leaving so she was  definitely in a fight it wasn't a  dominating fight like a lot of people  are making it out to be  um  yeah so  for all the people that are hating on  juliana fudge fudgy ufc welterweight  colby covington reportedly took seventh  place in a major south florida poker  tournament a tweet from annie slater  shows covington at the tournament and  gives more details on his reported  payout ufc star colby covington makes  final table of record-setting poker  tournament at hard rock hawley in  florida beating 7696  other entrants he gets 48  298 of the 2.5 million dollar prize pool  for finishing 7th  espn's brett akamoto tweeted about a  reported new addition to the ufc 280 in  abu dhabi according to his sources  muhammad mohayev will take on malcolm  gordon in abu dhabi on october 22nd  muhammad mohave has his next date and  opponent mohaya vs malcolm gordon agreed  to for ufc 280 in abu dhabi per sources  gordon on a two-fight win streak  muhammad most recently fought at ufc  london on july 23rd where he won in a  three-round decision and made headlines  after by taking shots at paddy pimblet's  character  jake paul's most valuable promotions  business partner nakisa bidarian  responded to dana white's comments about  the cancelled bout between jake paul and  haseem rahman jr at the ufc 277 post  fight press conference white theorized  that the fight was cancelled due to low  ticket sales and advised paul to  surround himself with better business  partners bidarian a former ufc  accountant responded to white in an  instagram story we're supposed to be  here saturday for a big fight but we had  to cancel driven by fighter health and  safety and liability potential we will  be back we are working on it it had zero  to do with ticket sales we already sold  more tickets more gate than ryan garcia  just did at staples center we were going  to be top 10 in gates since 2005 for  boxing at madison square garden and jake  paul was taking a big challenge all of  his fights have been at about 188 to 191  pounds and all of his opponents outside  of nate robinson have been plus or minus  one to two pounds of him they can try to  change the narrative they can try to  destroy what this young man has done i'm  proud of him he's his own boss he's his  own promoter and i'm just an accountant  ufc heavyweight tom aspinall gave his  fans an update on his knee injury that  he suffered 15 seconds into his  headlining bout with curtis blades at  ufc london on july 23rd in the video  aspinal revealed that he sustained heavy  damage to the knee tearing both his mcl  and his meniscus as well as inflicting  damage on the acl aspinall posted the  video right before heading into surgery  in london  morning everybody  today is surgery day i'm in london right  now and uh  absolutely starving because okay before  surgery and um  yeah i have suffered a torn mcl  a  meniscus and  some acl damage so i'm going to get that  fixed today but just a quick message  just to say thank you for all the  support really appreciate it i've had so  much love since the accident  and i'll see everybody on the side peace  out tuesday night dana white's contender  series returned for its second week of  season six after the season premiere  featured lackluster bouts and only one  contract awarded white urged future  competitors to step it up and they did  just that only one of the five bouts  tuesday went to decision and white was  so impressed with the performances he  awarded contracts to all five of the  winners in the featured bout chris  duncan knocked out charlie campbell in  the first round after being close to  getting finished himself in his  post-fight press conference duncan  talked about being on his heels during  the fight but knowing what he needed to  do to secure the contract i made a bit  of a mess of it but it's not how you  start it's how you finish he was rushing  in i watched some footage on him a while  ago and when he starts to get his groove  he starts weaving and bobbing with his  hands i saw him doing that and i just  got my head off the center line and just  threw my cannon and threw it right to  his chops i bounced his head off the  canvas putting someone down like that is  never nice but that's what i'm going for  and i knew that's what was going to  secure me my contract  aside from duncan the contract winners  are vinicius salvador francis marshall  waldo cortez acosta and billy gough  after the event dana personally  congratulated each winner  what a night congrats  this is what i'm talking about  you know on the internet we're number  two worldwide wow so do you remember  what i told you i said this is your gift  thank you  looking for more original mma content  check out